// Title: Potential APT Mustang Panda Activity Against Australian Gov
// Sigma ID: 7806bb49-f653-48d3-a915-5115c1a85234
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, G0129
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects specific command line execution used by Mustang Panda in a targeted attack against the
//   Australian government as reported by Lab52
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://lab52.io/blog/new-mustang-pandas-campaing-against-australia/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2023/TA/Mustang-Panda-Australia-Campaign/proc_creation_win_apt_mustang_panda_indicators.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "copy SolidPDFCreator.dll" and ProcessCommandLine contains "C:\\Users\\Public\\Libraries\\PhotoTvRHD\\SolidPDFCreator.dll") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "reg " and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run" and ProcessCommandLine contains "SolidPDF" and ProcessCommandLine contains "C:\\Users\\Public\\Libraries\\PhotoTvRHD\\")
